      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "In bifurcation lesion, a precise evaluation of lesion severity and disease extension requires the use of bifurcation (three branches) quantitative coronary angiography. The use of Intravascular imaging to guide PCI in bifurcation has shown to reduce clinical events. Selection and duration of the dual antiplatelet therapy after bifurcation lesion PCI require further investigation."
